class.description:
[LocalizedText] describes a text by its translation [member key] and [member context], fills its [code]{name}[/code] placeholders from [member args] and [TextInsertionServer], and picks the plural form from [member count_argument]. [method get_text] returns the current text.
Bound to a property of a node (for example [member Label.text], [member Button.text], [member RichTextLabel.text], [member Control.tooltip_text]), it sets that property again only when its text can have changed: when the locale of its channel changes ([signal TranslationServer.locale_changed]), when a value used by its placeholders changes ([signal TextInsertionServer.value_changed]), when catalogs change ([signal LocalizationServer.catalogs_changed]) or when one of its own properties changes. Refreshes are collected and run once at the end of the frame; a property is only set when its text is different.
A binding is the node metadata [code]localized_<property>[/code]: [code]localized_text[/code] binds [code]text[/code], [code]localized_tooltip_text[/code] binds [code]tooltip_text[/code]. Add it in the inspector with [b]Add Metadata[/b] (type [Object], then create or pick a [LocalizedText]), or call [method bind]. Metadata bindings are applied when the node enters the scene tree at run time (not in the editor) and removed when it leaves.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
# An NPC greeting: "Hello {player_name}!" in the catalog.
var greeting = LocalizedText.new()
greeting.key = &"NPC_GREETING"
greeting.bind($GreetingLabel)
TextInsertionServer.set_value(&"player_name", "Ada") # The label shows "Hello Ada!".

# A HUD line with a plural: "{enemy.count} enemy left" / "{enemy.count} enemies left".
var enemies = LocalizedText.new()
enemies.key = &"ENEMIES_LEFT"
enemies.count_argument = &"enemy.count"
enemies.bind($EnemiesLabel)
TextInsertionServer.set_value(&"enemy.count", 3) # "3 enemies left"
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
// An NPC greeting: "Hello {player_name}!" in the catalog.
var greeting = new LocalizedText();
greeting.Key = "NPC_GREETING";
greeting.Bind(GetNode<Label>("GreetingLabel"));
TextInsertionServer.SetValue("player_name", "Ada"); // The label shows "Hello Ada!".

// A HUD line with a plural: "{enemy.count} enemy left" / "{enemy.count} enemies left".
var enemies = new LocalizedText();
enemies.Key = "ENEMIES_LEFT";
enemies.CountArgument = "enemy.count";
enemies.Bind(GetNode<Label>("EnemiesLabel"));
TextInsertionServer.SetValue("enemy.count", 3); // "3 enemies left"
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
A bound node gets [constant Node.AUTO_TRANSLATE_MODE_DISABLED] so its text is not translated twice; the previous [member Node.auto_translate_mode] comes back when its last binding is removed. Other text properties of that node are then not translated automatically either: bind them with their own [LocalizedText].
Keys that no [TextLocalizationCatalog] has are looked up in the [TranslationDomain] of the channel, so [Translation] resources keep working.
[b]Note:[/b] Bindings and refreshes run on the main thread. [method get_text] can be called on any thread.
